# Third-party notices

## Specifications and codec references

- The baseline and interchange format are defined by ITU-T Recommendation T.87 (06/98), equivalent to ISO/IEC 14495-1. The Annex A procedures and Annex C syntax informed the MoonBit implementation. T.81 Annex B provides the referenced high-level marker syntax. The standards and original ITU distribution are owned by their respective copyright holders and are downloaded separately for review. [T.87](https://www.itu.int/rec/T-REC-T.87-199806-I/en) · [T.81](https://www.itu.int/rec/T-REC-T.81/en)
- CharLS 2.4.5, peeled Git commit `14b654dff1efed4d04e278ff3e99f0a486cf20cc`, is the independent reference. The core consults its scan, context and trait sources for cross-checking details. The codec runtime does not link CharLS. `imagecodecs` provides the prebuilt native oracle and PNG comparator. Its project license is BSD-3-Clause and its distributed wheels contain their own bundled-library license notices. [Pinned CharLS](https://github.com/team-charls/charls/tree/14b654dff1efed4d04e278ff3e99f0a486cf20cc) · [CharLS license](tests/fixtures/CHARLS_LICENSE.txt) · [imagecodecs license](https://github.com/cgohlke/imagecodecs/blob/v2026.11.11/LICENSE)
- Official `@team-charls/charls-wasm@0.10.0` is a second build of the same reference implementation. The Wasm package commit is `7b95b8fcbb3c9bd9183d02820c736afb63fcd2c4`. Its `extern/charls` points to `5a2481fb28573149e72621aefaabf5aa9eaf0eb1`. [Package source](https://github.com/team-charls/charls-wasm/tree/7b95b8fcbb3c9bd9183d02820c736afb63fcd2c4) · [Wasm license](tests/fixtures/CHARLS_WASM_LICENSE.txt)

## Data and consumers

- Official conformance images are fetched on demand from the pinned CharLS tree. Retain the rights and attribution accompanying the original ITU-T/ISO/IEC distribution. They are used for verification only. The repository contains no conformance raster copies. [Pinned conformance notes](https://github.com/team-charls/charls/tree/14b654dff1efed4d04e278ff3e99f0a486cf20cc/test/conformance)
- Synthetic images are generated by `scripts/corpus.py`, `core/stream_wbtest.mbt` and `web/pgm.mjs`. The seed and parameters are part of the source or verification reports.
- The fluorescence microscopy benchmark uses a channel crop of Lily of the Valley, distributed CC0 by scikit-image, downloaded as a TIFF with SHA-256 `395c2f0194c25b9824a8cd79266920362a0816bc9e906dd392adce2d8309af03`. [Dataset source](https://gitlab.com/scikit-image/data/-/blob/2cdc5ce89b334d28f06a58c9f0ca21aa6992a5ba/lily-of-the-valley-fluorescence.tif)
- The lunar elevation data derives from the Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter LOLA measurements and is attributed to NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio and visualizer Ernie Wright. The SVS public-domain data is downloaded and checked separately. [Lunar data provenance](tests/fixtures/LUNAR_DATA.md)
- `moonbitstack/moonimage@0.2.1` is fetched for the independent example only, under Apache-2.0. `playwright-core@1.65.1` (Apache-2.0) drives browser verification. [MoonImage license](https://github.com/moonbitstack/moonimage/blob/4f34b3d2680bdc144a9b082386fe02c9484a158f/LICENSE) · [Playwright license](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/main/LICENSE)
